{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-18T03:46:00.556Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"grok-4.6","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"6a20d4f8145bf05627aeff92","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"grok-4.6","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-crgk"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Ship the merge-driver install step as the canonical pm-ops/merge-driver export"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Every fleet package installs pm field-aware git merge drivers from its npm prepare script because Git never clones .git/config. Twelve consumer repos currently vendor a byte-identical untyped untested JavaScript prepare-merge-driver.mjs, which the TypeScript-only rule forbids. pm-ops already solved this shape for publish attestation: one canonical implementation, thin per-repo launchers. This feature makes merge-driver install the same: a typed, tested pm-ops/merge-driver export that resolves the real pm launcher, skips cleanly when pm is absent, fails loudly when a present CLI cannot install, and honours Windows PATHEXT/quoting through an injectable process boundary."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-18T03:46:00.556Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-18T03:46:00.556Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"package.json exports ./merge-driver with types ./dist/merge-driver.d.ts and default ./dist/merge-driver.js; runPrepareMergeDriver is the documented export: missing pm exits 0 with a one-line notice; a present CLI whose pm merge install fails exits non-zero with that command's output; Windows PATH quoting and PATHEXT shims are honoured via the injectable installer and platform parameter without faking the POSIX path; tests create temp git repos under mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), \"pm-ops-merge-\" )), run against the real pinned node_modules/.bin/pm binary, and assert merge.*.driver git config entries appear; tests cover missing-pm, non-executable-candidate, directory-candidate, broken-pm (a real script that exits 1), and Windows-shim paths; coverage remains 100/100/100/100 and the docstring gate reports zero violations"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"afb47a3d6e3164870bd8001e6635b2561cc82dbcc6944dcce4b4cfeaeab7dca8","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"909a7265eeb57dfda6ab3408a64e55d405fab2d588f1134af72986fc1d6d31ff"}
